{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - Given the lack of information about any proposals to reposition or alter the existing extraction equipment or flues associated with the commercial uses at ground floor, and in view of the increased occupancy proposed at the site, the application fails to comply with the intent of London Plan Policy D13 as it fails to show that the development would not prejudice the ongoing viability and operations of the commercial parade at ground level through potential complaints from future residents. ",
    "Reason : 2 - As a result of the significant scale and bulk of the mansard extension and the incongruous and overbearing hip-to-gable element proposed, the proposal would cause significant harm to the character and appearance of the subject property and wider area and to the symmetry and visual coherence of the Station Parade retail parade, contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2 and SC7 and the intent of the Residential Extension Guidelines",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal would provide a substandard quality of accommodation, both internally and externally, contrary to Local Plan policy SC5.",
    "Reason : 4 - In the absence of information on precise occupancy numbers and the associated cycle storage, waste and recycling and car parking requirements for the site, including detail as to where suitable facilities would be located, the proposals fail to comply with the intent of Local Plan policy EC2 as they do not show that parking, access and servicing needs have been suitably accounted for or that highway safety and parking conditions in the area would not be prejudiced as a result of the development. "
  ],
